# .harness/project.env: what the harness cannot infer. Written by `harness new`,
# read by `harness md` (CLAUDE.md, settings.json, kit), `harness build`, `harness run`.
# POSIX sh syntax. Edit, then `harness md`; a tool change also needs `harness build`
# and `harness run --fresh`.

# One line: what this project is. Rendered as `## Project` in CLAUDE.md.
PURPOSE="@@PURPOSE@@"

# Cluster or provider context, empty if none (e.g. "Talos Linux homelab, Cilium, Argo CD").
CLUSTER="@@CLUSTER@@"

# Tools baked into the image, from tools/ORDER. Languages detected in main/
# (go.mod, package.json, pyproject.toml, manifests, *.tf) are added at every `harness md`.
TOOLS="@@TOOLS@@"
